// expect-error: pin(call_arena) cannot hold: this value is not served by that arena
// expect-error: call sites, and a bracketed callee may have exactly one outside the region
//
// SPEC 5.4.1 for a *placement* pin, on the exact regression SPEC 5.2.1.1 admits
// it is silent about.
//
// Regime (a) brackets a call only while every call site of the callee is inside
// the region that brackets it. `make` has two and **one of them is outside
// `call_arena`**, so the bracket is dropped and every allocation in `make` goes
// back to the heap. **Nothing else about this program changes**: it still
// compiles, still returns the same value, still passes every other test in this
// suite, and runs slower. That is the failure mode SPEC 5.2.1.1 asks the
// manifest to record, and the reason a record is not enough -- somebody has to
// read the diff.
//
// The outside call's result is **discarded**, and that is load-bearing: a
// binding out here would hold the loop's sites as well, obligation 3 would
// reject the bracket too, and this fixture would stop being about regime (a).
//
// `pin(call_arena)` is that fact asserted, so the build stops here instead.
//
// **Delete the outside call and this program compiles** -- and so does moving it
// *inside* the region, which is what makes this fixture discriminate rather than
// merely fail. The test runner performs the
// inverse edit on `test_63_placement_pin.psm` -- a program known to compile --
// and requires the mutant to be rejected, so neither direction rests on a reader
// believing this comment.
//
// The error is at the `let`, one function away from the edit that caused it, and
// the note is what closes that distance: it names `make`, its call-site count and
// the obligation. A diagnostic that only said "not served" would send a reader
// looking for a missing `region` in a function that never had one.

struct Cmd {
    id: Int,
    weight: Int
}

fn make(i: Int) -> Cmd {
    let pin(call_arena) c = Cmd { id: i, weight: i * 2 }
    return c
}

fn main() -> Int {
    let mut total = 0
    // The whole of the regression. One more call, **outside** the region, so the
    // body would have to allocate from the arena on four paths and from the heap
    // on this one. Discarded, so obligation 3 is untouched and nothing but the
    // regime separates this from `test_63_placement_pin.psm`.
    make(99)
    region call_arena {
        let mut i = 0
        while (i < 4) {
            let keep = make(i)
            total = total + keep.id
            i = i + 1
        }
    }
    return total - total
}
